# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
/test-results
/playwright-report
/blob-report
# machine-local Playwright browser binary cache — redirected here (rather
# than the default %USERPROFILE%\AppData\Local\ms-playwright) because the
# C: drive has ~0 bytes free (see PROGRESS.md decision log, npm
# cache/tmp redirect entry, same root cause). Set via
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=E:\playwright-browsers when running
# `npx playwright install` / `npx playwright test` on this machine.
/playwright-browsers

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files - the .example template is a safe, secret-free reference
# and should stay tracked so collaborators/cloud agents know what's needed
.env*
!.env.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# local permission/trust settings - machine-specific, not for the cloud
# routine or collaborators to inherit automatically. .claude/agents/ (the
# job descriptions) stays tracked; only the settings files are ignored.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ephemeral scratch space: screenshots agents take against the local dev
# server to visually self-check UI slices (see AGENTS.md "UI
# self-verification"), plus one-off manual verification scripts (e.g.
# apply-migration.mjs) agents write to check something against the live
# DB by hand - never a build artifact to commit. If a check needs to be
# repeatable, it belongs in a real test file under a __tests__/ dir, not
# here.
/tmp/
